LOK Calc: an AutoFilter on marked rows keeps to those rows

Each time the filter list opens, GetFilterEntries grows an unnamed
filter range to the data rows right under it (ExtendDataArea and
ExtendBackColorArea), so appended rows join. It cannot tell them from
a totals row that was there when the user marked the block: the
total joined the filter, showed in its list and hid with the data.
Under LOK, an AutoFilter set on a marked block that spans rows keeps
that block: ScDBData remembers it (not saved) and never extends.

